---
import { fillFacts } from '../../lib/facts.mjs';
import Chapter from './Chapter.astro';
import { getProjects } from '../../lib/collections';

const items = await getProjects();
---
<Chapter n={9} title="Appendix" id="appendix">
  <p class="ap-note codex-measure" data-reveal>
    Systems work: where models stop being isolated learners and become
    architectures. The chapters above concern what a model learns; these
    concern how intelligence is assembled across vision, language models,
    vision-language models, and retrieval through model architecture,
    multimodal integration, retrieval pipelines, reranking, inference, and
    evaluation. The discipline is no longer only about learning
    representations, but about designing systems that can perceive, retrieve,
    reason, and answer.
  </p>
  <ol class="ap" data-reveal-stagger>
    {items.map((it) => (
      <li class="ap-item">
        <h3 class="ap-title">{it.data.title}</h3>
        <p class="ap-body">{fillFacts(it.data.summary)}</p>
        {(it.data.link || it.data.repo) && (
          <p class="ap-go">
            {it.data.link && (
              <a class="ap-btn" href={it.data.link}>
                {it.data.linkLabel ?? 'Open'}
                <span class="ap-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
              </a>
            )}
            {/* Quieter than the button on purpose: opening the thing is the
                first invitation, reading it is the second. */}
            {it.data.repo && (
              <a class="ap-src" href={it.data.repo} rel="noopener">Source</a>
            )}
          </p>
        )}
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>
</Chapter>

<style>
  .ap-note {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
  }
  .ap-go { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .ap-src {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--brass) 55%, transparent);
    padding-bottom: 1px;
  }
  .ap-src:hover { color: var(--fundus); border-bottom-color: var(--fundus); }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .ap-src { transition: color 200ms var(--ease-out), border-color 200ms var(--ease-out); }
  }
  .ap { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 1.6rem; max-width: 58rem; }
  .ap-item {
    border-top: var(--rule) solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--brass) 34%, transparent);
    padding-top: 0.9rem;
  }
  .ap-title {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-variant-caps: all-small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    font-size: var(--t-base);
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
  }
  .ap-body { font-size: var(--t-sm); line-height: 1.7; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; max-width: 66ch; }

  /* Only a project with somewhere to go carries one of these, so the button
     itself is the signal that there is something to open. */
  .ap-go { margin: 0.7rem 0 0; }
  .ap-btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.5ch;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.9rem;
    border: var(--rule) solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--brass) 60%, transparent);
    background: var(--paper-raised);
    transition: background 120ms ease, border-color 120ms ease;
  }
  .ap-btn:hover,
  .ap-btn:focus-visible {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brass) 12%, var(--paper-raised));
    border-color: var(--brass);
  }
  .ap-arrow { transition: transform 120ms ease; }
  .ap-btn:hover .ap-arrow { transform: translateX(2px); }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .ap-btn, .ap-arrow { transition: none; }
    .ap-btn:hover .ap-arrow { transform: none; }
  }
</style>
